# 🚀 Day 01: PowerShell Fundamentals for SysAdmins

Today marks the beginning of my 10-day PowerShell automation journey! I focused on understanding core PowerShell architecture, cmdlet naming conventions, and fundamental administration commands within **Windows Server 2022**.

---

## 📌 Key Learning Areas
* 🔹 **PowerShell Architecture & Versions:** Understanding the environment and system variables.
* 🔹 **Cmdlet Naming Conventions:** Learning the standard `Verb-Noun` syntax (e.g., `Get-Process`, `Set-ExecutionPolicy`).
* 🔹 **Command Discovery & Documentation:** Exploring commands dynamically using `Get-Command` and `Get-Help`.
* 🔹 **PowerShell Execution Policies:** Understanding script execution permissions and security configurations.

---

## 💻 Hands-on Exercises & Scripts

### 1. PowerShell Version Check
Displays detailed version details including PSVersion (5.1) and PSEdition.
```powershell
$PSVersionTable
--------
2. System Information Gathering
Retrieves computer name, OS product name, and current Windows version.
Get-ComputerInfo | Select-Object CsName, WindowsProductName, WindowsVersion.
------------
3. Service Inspection
Lists all registered Windows services along with their current status (Running/Stopped).
Get-Service
-------------
4. Process Monitoring
Retrieves running system processes along with handle counts, memory usage (WS/PM), and CPU time.
Get-Process
